# tools/d/drey_witness.rish -- the whole Mikrophone firmware journey, every rung proven in one command.
#
# Chapter A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) - waymark mikrophone - Mikrophone firmware journey - aggregate witness.
# Front door: mikrophone/README.md.
#
# The Mikrophone firmware journey grew from one crux -- a session that forgets. Each rung has its own witness, and this
# one runs every rung in rung order and asserts each GREEN, so the whole journey proves from cold in a single command --
# the reference weave the front door names.
#
# THE COUNT IS NOT WRITTEN HERE, ON PURPOSE. This header once said `eleven proven rungs` and recited all eleven by name,
# and the printed banner below once named the range `mikrophone` through `mikrophone`. The file ran SIXTEEN rungs by then. A count
# typed into a comment stops moving the day it is typed, while the legs below keep being added -- REDS %110 and %93 taught
# that for the ledger's own headline, %385 for the session-log shelves, and %386 books it here. So the roll call lives in
# one place only: the closing GREEN line, which names each rung it just ran. To count them, ask the file rather than
# this sentence:
#   grep -c '^let .* = run \[' tools/d/drey_witness.rish
#
# THE REFUSAL IS PROVEN, not merely written. `tools/fixtures/d/drey_witness_control.sh` plants a
# failing mikrophone and watches this roster exit non-zero, then all sixteen rungs passing and watches
# it exit zero -- both directions, one pen, so the asserts below are a demonstrated refusal rather
# than an inherited one. That control is what keeps this roster out of the redleg scan's no-marker
# count.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/drey_witness.rish

say "drey: Language EN -- the whole Mikrophone firmware journey, each rung's witness run in rung order and asserted GREEN in one command; the closing line names every rung it ran."
say "drey: Style Radiant — a device that forgets on purpose, proven whole: a capture held only while powered, kept only on a deliberate commit, redacted where a keeper strikes it, carried only when committed, and received only once proven — no byte crossing that a keeper did not need, none kept that cannot be proven."
say "drey: Lens TAME — every rung is pure Rye on the bench, bounded, invariant-asserted, refusing by name; no disk, no network, no key, no funds. Serving over a real transport stays the Comlink-served gate; real hardware stays custody gate %2."

let session = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/d/drey_session_witness.rish"]
assert session.ok else "drey: mikrophone session witness failed"
assert (session.out contains "GREEN drey-session") else "drey: mikrophone session not GREEN"

let wire = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/d/drey_wire_witness.rish"]
assert wire.ok else "drey: mikrophone wire witness failed"
assert (wire.out contains "GREEN drey-wire") else "drey: mikrophone wire not GREEN"

